<article class="env-remark" id="01FX">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01FX">Remark <span data-tag="01FX">4.5.6.7</span>.</a> Let $q: X \rightarrow S$ be an isofibration of simplicial sets. Then $q$ is an inner fibration: that is, it has the right lifting property with respect to every horn inclusion $\Lambda ^{n}_{i} \hookrightarrow \Delta ^{n}$ for $0 &lt; i &lt; n$ (such inclusions are categorical equivalences, by virtue of Corollary <a data-tag="01EJ" href="/tag/01EJ">4.5.4.14</a>). In particular, for each vertex $s \in S$, the fiber $X_{s} = \{ s\}  \times _{S} X$ is an $\infty $-category (Remark <a data-tag="01BF" href="/tag/01BF">4.1.1.6</a>). Moreover, if $S$ is an $\infty $-category, then $X$ is also an $\infty $-category (Remark <a data-tag="01BJ" href="/tag/01BJ">4.1.1.9</a>). </p>
